On his role in the transmission of the Mūlamadhyamakakārikā (ID:3715) and Prasannapadā (ID:3724) to Tibet, see [LF4HXHGF] (in particular p. 649).</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3749"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ratnagotravibhāga</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rātnagotravibhāga mahāyānottaratantraśāstra</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">uttaratantra</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po rgyud bla ma'i bstan bcos</title><author ref="person:3747">maitreya</author><author ref="person:3756">asaṅga</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The authorship of the work comes to be ascribed to the future Buddha Maitreya (ID:3747) in the Indian tradition from the 11th c. onward and in the Tibetan tradition. On earlier witnesses ascribing the authorship to Sāramati or Sthiramati, see [BAQ9MH4T]: 20-27. No attribution of that work to Asaṅga (ID:3756) was located in Indian sources, but the colophon of the Tibetan translation by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab ascribes the verses to Maitreya and the prose commentary to Asaṅga ([BAQ9MH4T]: 27-28).&#13;
There are six Tibetan translations, only that by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab and Sajjana is currently extant ([BAQ9MH4T]: chap. 6).</note><idno type="APIS">3749</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5476"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po rgyud bla ma'i TIk+ka de nyid snang ba</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཐེག་པ་ཆེན་པོ་རྒྱུད་བླ་མའི་ཊཱིཀྐ་དེ་ཉིད་སྣང་བ</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1390-01-01" notAfter="1390-12-31">1390</date><author ref="person:4125">gha rung pa lha'i rgyal mtshan</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Date of composition: ston pa 'das nas lo nyis stong nyis rgya dang nyer gsuM song ba'i dus = 1390.</note><relatedItem type="commentaryOn" target="work:3749"/><idno type="APIS">5476</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work7338"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">(undefined/undetermined)</title><idno type="APIS">7338</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work7639"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos rje jo nang pa kun mkhyen chen po'i rnam thar</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཆོས་རྗེ་ཇོ་ནང་པ་ཀུན་མཁྱེན་ཆེན་པོའི་རྣམ་ཐར</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1361-01-01" notAfter="1401-12-31">after 1361 before 1401</date><author ref="person:4125">gha rung pa lha'i rgyal mtshan</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><idno type="APIS">7639</idno></bibl></listBibl><listPlace><place xml:id="place5732"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dben gnas nam mkha' mdzod</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">དབེན་གནས་ནམ་མཁའ་མཛོད</placeName><idno type="APIS">5732</idno></place></listPlace><listRelation><relation xml:id="rel7754" name="lineage-predecessor-of" active="#person4213" passive="#person4125" type="uncertain"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex113022026-01-2622-34-04"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel5835" name="student-of" active="#person4125" passive="#person4213" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel5836" name="student-of" active="#person4125" passive="#person4128" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel2233" name="active-at" active="#person4125" passive="#place5732" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel7148" name="student-of" active="#person4125" passive="#person6741" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel1163" name="author-of" active="#person4125" passive="#work5476" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex113022025-02-2416-01-14"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel6369" name="author-of" active="#person4125" passive="#work7639" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel2232" name="composed-at" active="#work5476" passive="#place5732" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex113022025-02-2416-01-14"/></desc></relation></listRelation></standOff><text>
